				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				874,
				6
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Add LRU cache for FindFiles and optimize dev_log for release\n\nImplement an LRU cache for FindFilesInWorkspace to reduce latency during\nfuzzy file matching. The cache uses a 2.5s TTL and 128-entry capacity with\nsimple eviction, short-circuiting repeated walks during Cmd+P typing bursts\nthat typically fire 5-10 calls in 200ms.\n\nAdditionally, gate the dev_log! macro body on cfg!(debug_assertions) so it\nbecomes a literal no-op in release builds via LLVM dead-code-elimination.\nThis removes the format!, IsEnabled lookup, file-sink write, and dedup-\nmutex lock from the hot IPC path while preserving compile-time type-checking\nof format arguments.\n\nAlso revert the verbose development naming back to simple \"Mountain\" for\nbinary, lib, identifier, and productName, and remove obsolete .Backup files.",
			"SHA": "5c123e3aa335f9078086b721f4fbbe75a1651167"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-25T01:22:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				876,
				11
			],
			"Message": "revert(Mountain): Revert Mountain naming to verbose development identifier\n\nRevert the Mountain binary/lib/tauri config from 'Mountain' back to the verbose development identifier 'DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_ElectronProfile_Mountain' to maintain continuity with existing build artifacts and CI configurations.\n\nAdditionally, implement SCM provider registration handlers pulled out of the language-providers catch-all:\n- Add `RegisterScmProvider` notification handler that wires through `SourceControlManagementProvider` trait and emits `sky://scm/register`\n- Add `RegisterScmResourceGroup` notification handler that seeds groups via `UpdateSourceControlGroup` trait and emits `sky://scm/registerGroup`\n- These previously fell through the language-provider OR-block which never populated `ApplicationState::SourceControl`, leaving the SCM viewlet empty\n\nAlso:\n- Add `WalkUpToProjectRoot` to CliParse that walks up from build dirs to find project markers (Cargo.toml, package.json, .git, etc.)\n- Trust Sky/Target, Output/Target, and Dependency paths in PathSecurity for bundled extensions\n- Add benign ENOENT substrings for gitlens, copilot, claude-code, roo-cline, vim registers, and bundled product.json probes\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Binary and lib names changed from 'Mountain' to the verbose development identifier.",
			"SHA": "6c908b6eaa9030c30ee11f705f016f38ae2b3428"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-25T00:42:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Implement configuration target support and clean up naming\n\nImplement missing ConfigurationTarget handling in UpdateValue.rs:\n- UserLocal now maps to User settings.json (Land has no sync backend)\n- WorkspaceFolder writes to <folder>/.vscode/settings.json for first folder\n- Memory target stores in-memory only (no disk write)\n- Default and Policy targets return read-only errors per spec\n\nAdditionally:\n- Revert binary/lib names from verbose dev identifier back to \"Mountain\"\n- Simplify Tauri identifier to \"land.editor.binary\" and productName to \"Mountain\"\n- Remove duplicate externalBin entry and obsolete .Backup files\n\nThis completes the ConfigurationProvider trait implementation for all VS Code configuration targets, enabling extensions to persist settings to user preferences, workspace .vscode folders, and in-memory session state.",
			"SHA": "1c3dd9e7d4dde40184a53712500b91c447eb2197"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1779025693087
}